+# Review selection controls
+
+## Intent
+
+Reviewers select one or more pending items before explicitly approving them. Nothing is confirmed by rendering or selection alone.
+
+## States and controls
+
+- Each pending item renders as a native button with `aria-pressed="false"`; selecting it changes only that button to `aria-pressed="true"`.
+- The **Approve selected** native button is disabled until one or more items are selected.
+- Approving marks only the selected items confirmed, clears every pressed state, and disables Approve selected again.
+- An empty queue remains usable: it contains no item controls and its approval control stays disabled.
+
+## Accessibility and responsive behavior
+
+Use native buttons so keyboard activation, focus, and pressed semantics are supplied by the browser. The controls remain in normal document flow, so they wrap rather than clip on narrow viewports. No image or icon assets are required.
